      "message": "[runtime-v2-promotion] Finish recovered production arbiter adapter corrections\n\nContinue the original recovered eight-path implementation on exact ce42573.\nUse validated durable finalized frontiers, not deletable receipts, and credit\nnon-record housekeeping only to its own native durable maintenance progress.\nPersist unserviced non-record obligations across restart; preserve existing\nsource-clock episodes and reject missing current authority. Preserve a final\narchive receipt across cooperative yield without duplicate publishing or record\nprogress; surface completed maintenance errors during concurrent stop/drain.\n\nOne production owner-entry arbiter; no independent retention loop or fixed\narchive:retirement ratio. Original source/urgent priority, single worker, <=512\narchive slices, native retention bounds, 240-second residence, 120-source-second\nrecovery, workload and strategy/policy/acceptance bytes are unchanged.\n\n286 focused/integrated/storage/control tests passed locally on Python 3.13.5,\nzero failures/errors/skips. All four native assemblies import/collect; complete\nprepared-byte and policy checks passed. These are NOT frozen-environment or\ncapacity qualification. This commit is a durable exact-source checkpoint.\nThe required Python 3.12.14 / websockets 17.1 verification and one unchanged\nfour-trial cohort remain unused. No canonical, market, Phase F or deployment\nauthority is established. Detailed original and failed/passing logs accompany\nthe recovery package. Liveness is conditional on fresh demand, valid clock and\nservice leases, positive native progress and bounded owner delay.",
